  "description": "DAJVAN crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C107 H158 Ho4 O57,1.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho6 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho7 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho8 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.494-3.972 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.64-113.89°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho4(μ3-OH)4(η2-mgp)6(μ-η2-mgp)(μ-η2-Ac)(H2O)2]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
